    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Nicole calls these her stupid-simple dinner for nights when there is no time and nobody feels like cooking. They are on repeat in her house almost every week: her girls build their own bowls, and you get all the flavors of sushi night without the work.</p><p>Warm rice on one side, baby lettuces in a simple sesame dressing on the other, cubes of raw King Salmon down the middle, and a spread of toppings to finish. &ldquo;When it comes to fish, I want to know where it&rsquo;s coming from,&rdquo; Nicole says. &ldquo;Their seafood is traceable to named farms, their suppliers are third-party tested, and it takes the guesswork out of buying high-quality fish.&rdquo;</p><p>There is no right or wrong way to build one. Use what you love, skip what you don&rsquo;t, and make it your own.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
